 "spec": "to_csv_field(value, default="") returns a CSV-safe field for a single value. None and empty strings return default; a string is stripped, and if the result is empty it returns default, otherwise it is returned as is unless it contains a comma, double quote or newline, in which case it is wrapped in double quotes with internal quotes doubled. Ints and floats become str(value); any other type (e.g. list, dict) raises TypeError.",
 "reference": "def to_csv_field(value, default=""):
    if value is None:
        return default
    if isinstance(value, (int, float)):
        return str(value)
    if not isinstance(value, str):
        raise TypeError(f"unsupported type: {type(value).__name__}")
    text = value.strip()
    if not text:
